# validate-acceptance-bulk-stamp baseline — Research Lab
#
# Human Acceptance Records that declare `human-interactive` while naming the
# same acceptor at the same instant as another packet. The registry defines that
# method as a human exercising the delivered behavior in a live session, and one
# human cannot exercise two deliveries in one second, so each group below is a
# self-contradiction rather than a suspicion.
#
# Frozen so the guard can fail on a NEW bulk stamp while this pre-existing set is
# corrected by the workstreams that own it. NOTHING here is corrected by editing
# the record to make the guard quiet.
#
# Keyed `<packet>::<acceptedBy>@<acceptedAt>` — per RECORD, and INCLUDING the
# stamp. Both halves are load-bearing. Freezing the group would let a third packet
# join an already-frozen instant for free, which is the act being guarded. Dropping
# the stamp would let a frozen record be re-stamped into a different collision and
# stay silent. Keyed this way, a record that moves produces a key nobody froze.
#
# THIS LIST MUST SHRINK, NEVER GROW. An entry is paid down by one of:
#   - the acceptor performing the walk and recording the instant it happened, or
#   - relabelling the record to the method that actually applies, where the
#     acceptance happened elsewhere and `record` can point at it, or
#   - withdrawing a record whose acceptance did not happen
# Never by deleting a line here to make the run green.
#
# A baseline entry that no longer collides is reported STALE and the run still
# exits 0. Remove it. Do NOT regenerate the baseline to silence a new finding.
#
# Regenerate ONLY when deliberately accepting the current set:
#   node scripts/validate-acceptance-bulk-stamp.mjs --update-baseline
#
# There is no --skip / --force / --ignore / --bypass flag and there never will be.
# A bypass-shaped flag exits non-zero.
#
# FROZEN: 4 record(s) across 2 collision group(s), of 6 eligible `human-interactive` record(s) in 24 acceptance record(s), on 2026-08-25.
#
# ---- finding detail --------------------------------------------------------
#   specs/007-technical-analysis-decision-lab::operator@2026-08-19T19:04:11Z
#              declares `human-interactive` accepted by operator at 2026-08-19T19:04:11Z, the same instant as 1 other packet (specs/008-portfolio-survival-and-brief-lab)
#   specs/008-portfolio-survival-and-brief-lab::operator@2026-08-19T19:04:11Z
#              declares `human-interactive` accepted by operator at 2026-08-19T19:04:11Z, the same instant as 1 other packet (specs/007-technical-analysis-decision-lab)
#   specs/025-company-multi-horizon-intelligence-lab::operator@2026-08-23T18:26:55Z
#              declares `human-interactive` accepted by operator at 2026-08-23T18:26:55Z, the same instant as 1 other packet (specs/027-company-scoped-owner-deep-links)
#   specs/027-company-scoped-owner-deep-links::operator@2026-08-23T18:26:55Z
#              declares `human-interactive` accepted by operator at 2026-08-23T18:26:55Z, the same instant as 1 other packet (specs/025-company-multi-horizon-intelligence-lab)
